# STAT CAL — Project Overview

## Background

Statistical analysis often requires users to combine multiple tools, understand different analytical procedures, prepare datasets manually, and interpret statistical output.

STAT CAL was developed as an attempt to bring several common statistical workflows into a unified analytical environment.

---

## Objective

The primary objective of STAT CAL is to provide an accessible statistical analytics platform that guides users from dataset preparation through statistical analysis and interpretation.

---

## Core Analytical Areas

The platform focuses on:

1. Data preparation
2. Exploratory data analysis
3. Group comparison
4. Regression analysis
5. Forecasting
6. Statistical Process Control

---

## Development Focus

STAT CAL combines knowledge from several areas:

### Statistics

Application of statistical methods to real-world datasets.

### Data Analysis

Data preparation, exploration, modelling, and interpretation.

### Software Development

Designing an interactive application around analytical workflows.

### Data Visualisation

Presenting analytical results in a form that users can understand.

---

## Intended Users

The platform is intended to support users who need to perform statistical analysis but may not want to construct every analytical workflow manually.

Potential users include:

* Students
* Researchers
* Analysts
* Quality professionals
* Data-oriented professionals

---

## Project Status

STAT CAL is an active development project.

The current application is available through the live deployment:

https://stat-cal.vercel.app/

Future development will focus on expanding statistical functionality, improving analytical guidance, strengthening reporting capabilities, and improving the overall user experience.
